{"assets":["/editorial-assets/975f1441c993381416f009efc37a25eb5603a67698ad103d71a20cb5ad963084.png"],"contestId":"699","diagnostics":[{"code":"tutorial-known-absent","message":"699E","severity":"warning"},{"code":"tutorial-known-absent","message":"699F","severity":"warning"},{"code":"tutorial-known-absent","message":"698E","severity":"warning"}],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"New problems will be added as soon as the analysis is ready."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"699A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/699/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"699A - Launch of Collider"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To solve this problem it is enough to look at all pairs of adjacent particles such that the left particle will move to the right and the right particle will move to the left. If there is no such pair the answer is -1. Otherwise, let's iterate through the particles from the left to the right. If the particle "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will move to the right and the particle "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 will move to the left we know that this particles will be at the same point simultaneously, so we need to update the answer with value ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") / 2. The answer is always integer because all coordinates of the particles are even numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"699B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/699/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"699B - One Bomb"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To solve this problem we need to calculate two arrays "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"V"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[] and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[], where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"V"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] must be equal to the number of walls in the column number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] must be equal to the number of walls in the row number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also let's store the total number of walls in the variable "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cur"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we need to look over the cells. Let the current cell be ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Let's count the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cur"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — how many walls will destroy the bomb planted in the cell ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"): "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"V"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. If the cell ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") has a wall we count it twice, so we need to subtract 1 from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cur"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we found the answer and need to plant the bomb in the cell ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there is no such cell we need to print \"NO\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"699C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/699/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"699C - Vacations"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem can be solved with dynamic programming. Let's solve the opposite problem and find the maximum number of days which Vasya will not have a rest. We need o use two-dimensional array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] equals to the maximum number of days, which Vasya will not have a rest, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" days passed and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" 0, if Vasya had a rest during the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" 1, if Vasya participated in the contest on the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" 2, if Vasya went to gym on the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then the transitions for the day number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" look like:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][0] must be updated with maximum value of the array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the previous day; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if there will be a contest on the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day (i. e. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to 1 or 3), than we update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][1] with values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1][0] + 1 and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1][2] + 1; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if the gym is open on the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day (i. e. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to 2 or 3), than we update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][2] with values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1][0] + 1 and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1][1] + 1. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After that we need to choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from all values of the array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the last day and print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"699D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/699/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"699D - Fix a Tree"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One can easily see that given sequence describes a functional graph, thus a directed graph with edges going from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" for every "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". This graph represents a set of cycles and each cycle vertex is a root of its own tree (possibly consisting of one vertex). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/975f1441c993381416f009efc37a25eb5603a67698ad103d71a20cb5ad963084.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Picture above shows an example of a functional graph. It consists of two cycles 1, 6, 3 and 4. Vertex 6 is the root of the tree consisting of vertices 0, 2, 6 and 8, vertex 3 roots the tree of vertices 3 and 5, vertex 4 — root of tree of vertices 4 and 7 and vertex 1 forms a tree of only one vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In terms of functional graph, our goal is to make the graph consisting of exactly one cycle of exactly one vertex looped to itself."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Operation of change is equivalent to removing some outgoing edge and adding a new one, going to somewhat else vertex. Let's firstly make our graph containing only one cycle. To do so, one can choose any of initially presented cycles and say that it will be the only one. Then one should consider every other cycle, remove any of its in-cycle edges and replace it with an edge going to any of the chosen cycle's vertices. Thus the cycle will be broken and its vertices (along with tree ones) will be connected to the only chosen cycle. One will need to do exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cycleCount"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 such operations. Note that the removing of any non-cycle edge does not make sense, because it does not break any cycle."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next thing is to make the cycle length be equal to 1. That might be already satisfied, if one will choose a cycle of minimal length and this length equals 1. Thus, if the initial graph contains any cycle of length 1, we are done with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cycleCount"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 operations. Otherwise, the cycle contains more than one vertex. It can be fixed with exactly one operation — one just need to break any of in-cycle edges, say from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", and add an edge from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". The graph will remain consisting of one cycle, but consisting of one self-looped vertex. In that case, we are done with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cycleCount"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To do all the operations above, one can use DSU structure, or just a series of DFS. Note that there is no need in realisation of edge removing and creating, one just needs to analyze initial graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/46148"}